# Astro Component Patterns

All components in this project follow consistent patterns for props, translations, and structure.

## Component Structure

### Props Interface

Always define a typed `Props` interface and destructure from `Astro.props`:

```typescript
---
interface Props {
  lang: string;
}

const { lang } = Astro.props;
---
```

### Translation Loading

All components receive `lang: string` prop and load translations dynamically:

```typescript
const t = await import(`../i18n/${lang}.json`);
```

Then access translations via `t.namespace.key` (e.g., `t.hero.name`, `t.about.title`).

## Component Patterns

### Pages

Pages explicitly set the language:
- `src/pages/index.astro`: Sets `lang="en"` (English homepage at `/`)
- `src/pages/pl/index.astro`: Sets `lang="pl"` (Polish homepage at `/pl`)

Pages pass `lang` prop to all components they use.

### Scripts

- **Inline Scripts**: Use `<script is:inline>` for scripts that must run immediately (e.g., theme initialization)
- **Client Scripts**: Place client-side JavaScript at the bottom of the component, outside `<script is:inline>`
- **No Framework Scripts**: This project uses pure Astro, no React/Vue/Svelte components

### External Dependencies

- **Lottie Animations**: Loaded via CDN script in `Layout.astro`:
  ```html
  <script src="https://unpkg.com/@lottiefiles/dotlottie-wc@0.8.11/dist/dotlottie-wc.js" type="module"></script>
  ```

### Theme System

- Theme toggle uses `data-theme` attribute on `<html>` element
- Values: `"light"` or `"dark"`
- Theme preference stored in `localStorage` with key `"theme"`
- Theme initialization script in `Layout.astro` prevents flash of unstyled content

## Component Examples

### Basic Component

```astro
---
interface Props {
  lang: string;
}

const { lang } = Astro.props;
const t = await import(`../i18n/${lang}.json`);
---

<section class="my-component">
  <h1>{t.section.title}</h1>
</section>

<style>
  .my-component {
    /* Component-specific styles */
  }
</style>
```

### Component with Client Script

```astro
---
interface Props {
  lang: string;
}

const { lang } = Astro.props;
const t = await import(`../i18n/${lang}.json`);
---

<section class="interactive-component">
  <button id="toggle">Toggle</button>
</section>

<script>
  document.getElementById('toggle')?.addEventListener('click', () => {
    // Client-side logic
  });
</script>
```

## Important Rules

- ✅ Always type `Props` interface
- ✅ Always destructure props from `Astro.props`
- ✅ Always load translations with dynamic import
- ✅ Use scoped `<style>` blocks for component-specific CSS
- ✅ Place client scripts at the bottom of components
- ❌ Don't use React/Vue/Svelte components
- ❌ Don't use framework-specific features
